<title>UK: Rio Tinto hit by tumbling copper price.</title>
<headline>Rio Tinto hit by tumbling copper price.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mining group Rio Tinto Plc dropped in early trade on Thursday, in reaction to recent sharp falls in copper prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>A week after Rio shares scaled record highs on the back of copper price strength, the shares have taken a knock as the metal succumbed to a wave of selling that sent prices down to a seven-week low.</p>
<p>Rio shares were down 22p at 10.62 stg by 0747 GMT in volume of over half a million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the falling copper price that has done the damage,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
